  "summary_en": "Ontario regulation establishing a pilot project for testing automated vehicles (SAE Levels 3-5 and truck platooning) on public highways. It sets Registrar approval for testers, safety mechanisms, driver duties, collision reporting, $5M minimum insurance, and liability provisions. Consolidated to November 2025; revoked October 13, 2027.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Automated vehicles may be operated on highways only by owners approved by the Registrar for testing.",
   "Defines automated vehicles by SAE J3016 Levels 3, 4, 5 and co-operative truck platooning.",
   "Requires engage/disengage, failure alert and driver takeover or safe-stop mechanisms.",
   "Owners must carry minimum $5M liability insurance ($8M for vehicles seating eight or more).",
   "Owners must report collisions within 10 days and retain records; regulation revoked October 13, 2027."
  ],
